A classic example at the beginning of learning programming, written in Go.
`hello.go` is the source file; it is a command, so `command` is its rightmost label.

@[hello.go@=
@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/file@>
@

@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/package comment@=
// Command hello prints a greeting.
@

@<hello@:command@:Language@/Go@/File@/main body@=
fmt.Println("Hello, World!")
@~ Project@/hello@/topics@/output @
The command takes no flags and no positional arguments.
@<hello@:command@:UI@/Command Line@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'hello',
}
@